{
  "_doc": "EVENTS — public ICS calendar feeds for the Events tab. Every url below is copied VERBATIM from ea_cloud-calendar/data/calendars.json, which probed and item-counted each one by hand before adding it (see that file's `_doc_verified`/per-entry `verified` note) — not re-probed here, just re-used, same 'libs/core and libs/updater are byte-identical across ea_cloud-calendar and ea_cloud-news' precedent this repo already follows for whole modules, applied to one data file's rows instead. This is every entry from that file whose category is events/sports/observances/school/astro, PLUS every holidays entry — i.e. the full set (calendars.json currently has no category outside those six, so nothing was actually excluded by this filter; if a future calendars.json entry ships in a category this rule doesn't cover — e.g. a personal calendar — it should NOT be copied here without a deliberate decision). Parsed via IcsParser.kt (copied verbatim from ea_cloud-calendar/libs/cal — see that file's header comment), synced by EventsSync.kt (also a field-for-field port of that app's CalSync.kt, including its per-calendar refresh_hours throttle). Adding a calendar is an entry HERE plus a rebuild — no Kotlin change. Baked into BuildConfig.EVENTS_B64 by app/build.gradle, same pattern as data/topics.json/data/sources.json/data/media.json.",
  "_doc_fields": "id: stable key, also the cache filename. name: shown in the UI. url: ICS/webcal endpoint, copied verbatim from ea_cloud-calendar/data/calendars.json. category: holidays|astro|events|sports|observances|school — drives grouping/colour bucket. color: hex used for the event dot/chip. enabled: fetched at sync time. refresh_hours: per-feed override of defaults.refresh_hours.",
